To address path MTU discovery issues on your Nokia 7750 SR routers and enable dynamic TCP MSS adjustment based on ICMP feedback, configure the following for BGP sessions:

```
configure router
    bgp
        path-mtu-discovery
    exit
```

This command enables automatic path MTU adaptation by:
1. Setting the initial TCP session MTU to match the egress interface MTU
2. Enabling the DF (Don't Fragment) bit in TCP packets
3. Dynamically adjusting the MTU/MSS when ICMP fragmentation-needed messages are received
4. Optimizing throughput without manual path MTU configuration

For granular control, you can also apply this at the BGP group or neighbor level:
```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group_name>
            path-mtu-discovery
            neighbor <ip_address>
                path-mtu-discovery
```

The system will now automatically optimize packet sizes for all TCP sessions using BGP, ensuring efficient data transmission while preventing fragmentation-related session drops.
