To prevent iBGP-learned routes from being reflected back to their originators, configure each route reflector with a unique cluster ID and designate its clients within a BGP group. Use the following CLI command template:

```
configure router bgp group "CLIENT_GROUP" cluster <cluster-id>
```

Replace `"CLIENT_GROUP"` with the name of your BGP group containing route reflector clients, and `<cluster-id>` with a unique identifier (e.g., the router's loopback IP). This ensures routes are not propagated back to the advertising peer by leveraging the route reflector's inherent loop prevention using the `ORIGINATOR_ID` and `CLUSTER_LIST` attributes.

Example:
```
configure router bgp group "IBGP_CORE" cluster 192.168.0.1
``` 

Apply this configuration to all route reflectors in your network. Clients in the specified group will automatically be treated as route reflector clients, and routes learned from these peers will not be reflected back to them.
